  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-10T12:15:33.377Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a FX layer, which allows me to switch the 'Eye & Eyelids' setting between 'Animation' and 'Tracking' based on several conditions.\nThis way, I can disable blinking for some gestures or also, when I disable it with a bool parameter. In my use case, I want disable tracking on start.\nBut, if the conditions leads me to 'Eye Animation' state within the first seconds, the tracking will not be disabled. I see it in debug menu, that I am in the right state, but the tracking is still active then.\nAs workaround, I had to add a 'WaitForLoaded' state, which waits 5 seconds, until it switches to the 'Eye Animation' state.",
